WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.390
- As you all know, there
is a global situation

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.690
going on that affects the whole world.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:08.260
And of course, people
looking for jobs are affected

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.050
in a significant way right now as well.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.040
Most companies around the globe

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.480
have moved their recruiting
efforts to online formats.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.590
This is also true for consulting,

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.800
where the case studies,
behavioral interviews,

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.560
and other problem-solving games

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.980
now all take place in the online world.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:25.860
And this of course,

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.430
poses some new challenges to candidates.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:29.880
In this video, I'm going to share

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.420
how the recruiting processes
of MBB Consulting Firms,

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.700
this stands for McKinsey, BCG, Bain,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.280
but also other tier one,
tier two, consulting firms

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.880
do look like at the moment.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.620
For that I talked to several friends

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.500
who had interviews in these
firms in the last month

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.081
and also did a little Instagram
survey where I got lots

00:00:47.081 --> 00:00:50.480
of other impressions from people
literally around the world.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.710
So I'm first going to
describe how these interviews

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:53.910
look like at the moment,

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.330
but then also sharing a
couple of tips and tricks.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.630
What you can do to better
adapt to the situation,

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:00.400
hopefully improve your performance

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.410
in these interviews as much as possible.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.787
So welcome to another coffee
break here on my channel,

00:01:04.787 --> 00:01:07.430
"Firm Learning", my name is
Heinrich and on my channel

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.700
I want to help you to become successful

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.690
in the first years of your career.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.730
Though before we start, I
wanna make the disclaimer

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:16.830
that even within the same
firm, interview processes

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:19.600
can change significantly
country by country,

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.130
also office by office within one country.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:24.800
So as always, take this
information with a grain of salt,

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.220
though I do believe that there
are some valuable lessons

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.060
to be learned for most people applying

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.920
to consulting in these special times.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.020
So let's start not all.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.190
What many people reported is that most

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:38.230
of these consulting firms now
apply two tiered approach.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.850
They have some kind of
automated assessment going on

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.970
as a first step, and then
they conduct the more

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:46.040
well known regular
interviews as a second step

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:49.750
in some type of telephone or
video conference based format.

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:53.360
So let's jump into both of
these types, one after the other

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.450
and then let me share some
insights on them as well.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:58.000
So let's start with your
automated online assessment.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.180
Almost all of these consulting
firms have some kind

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.010
of digital tests like this going on.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.290
It's already pretty well known

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.510
as the McKinsey Problem Solving Game

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:06.840
where based on their information,

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.250
they ask you to balance out an ecosystem.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.650
Pretty much check how
well you can interact

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.600
with information presented
in tables and other forms

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.140
and a similar but maybe a
bit more traditional approach

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.360
is what BCG is doing

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.340
with their interactive online case.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.710
This again is where we will need

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:23.320
to answer different questions

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.585
but more in a case-based format,

00:02:25.585 --> 00:02:28.360
which more closely resembles
the case interviews

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.750
that you also known
from the main interviews

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.330
that you will then face
in the second step.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.337
So several people ask me,

00:02:33.337 --> 00:02:35.820
"Okay, Heinrich, what can
I do to prepare for that?"

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.450
This is not even the standard case format,

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:39.610
what can I really do there?

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.020
Isn't much material out there.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.590
And one type of prep
material that I found really

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.840
helpful for these types
of online assessments

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.380
is the GMAT Integrated
Reasoning Materials.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.690
So for the uninitiated
integrated reasoning

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.950
as a section of the GMAT test,

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:55.670
GMAT is a big standardized
computer-based test

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:56.790
that is needed for almost

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:59.220
all MBA programs to get admitted to them.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.420
And in this integrated reasoning section

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:04.950
you get different little
problems with graphs, with charts

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.810
which other information
that is presented to you.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:09.070
And then you are asked
to answer multiple choice

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:11.570
based questions based on these materials.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:13.070
And from everything
that I've seen or heard,

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:15.110
this is exactly the type of format

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:17.170
that is used by many of
these consulting firms.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.140
So if you are looking

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:20.430
for some widely available prep formats,

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.070
check out the Integrated
Reasoning Section of the GMAT,

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.840
you will find lots of books
on these topics online.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.520
So trust this can be helpful for you.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.740
The next point that many
people underestimate is

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.900
the time pressure that many
of these tests put you into.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.760
So often it's not the case
that you have open-ended time

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.610
but in the program, there
is a timer that runs down.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.230
And once the timer is at zero,

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.580
you will not be able to
answer any more questions.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.210
And of course as most of these tests

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:45.500
are multiple choice, you should

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.410
make sure that you get on to the very end,

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.340
because of, for instance

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:50.490
there are four answer options available

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:51.560
in the multiple choice.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.520
Then just, if you are guessing in the end

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.870
you still will be able to get
25% of the points, 25% right.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.100
So really do some time management.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.990
So practice this as well again here

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:03.933
the GMAT prep material
can be really helpful

00:04:03.933 --> 00:04:06.950
because there is where you
have these time-based tests.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.550
So make sure that at
some point you might just

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:11.110
accept to lose on a
question just to move on

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:13.780
because you do want to avoid
of spending all your time

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.150
on one of many, many questions
that you need to answer.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:18.540
And last year on the
online assessment section,

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:22.040
always look out for little
traps that they put out for you,

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.490
because of course they also want to test

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:25.580
how accurate you can think under pressure.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.160
So I've seen how many of these heads

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.120
rather are some little traps included.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.960
So for instance, you might be
required to multiply a number

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:33.480
with a certain percentage figure.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.123
And then this percentage
figure is stated as 0.03%.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:39.860
So I'd assume that many people would

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:42.733
just take the number
and multiply it by 0.03,

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:45.080
because they believe that if they do that,

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.870
they are multiplying it with 3%.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:50.303
But of course it's the
number is stated is 0.03%,

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:52.790
then you need to divide this number

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.740
by an additional hundred to actually

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:56.560
be able to multiply it correctly.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.490
So again, these little
things might seem obvious

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:00.930
but if you're under time
pressure looking at these tasks

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:03.150
this would exactly be the
things that you will miss.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.370
Another thing that I've seen is

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.600
that maybe there was
one number given to you,

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.900
maybe the cost of the
business in one year.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:10.600
And then there were lots
of information given

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.520
from what you needed to calculate the cost

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.840
of the business in the
other year, the next year

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.580
but then they didn't ask you
for the cost of the next year,

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.320
but they asked to for the difference

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:21.520
between the cost of the
first and the second year.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.150
So pretty much needed
to calculate the cost

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:25.130
for the second year and then subtract

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.820
the cost from the first year.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:27.973
And here again, I just
see with lots of people

00:05:27.973 --> 00:05:31.010
will just insert the total
cost for the second year

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.630
just because they were under pressure.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.470
Didn't read that accurately.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:38.430
So always take the time to
really precisely understand

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:40.130
what you really need to calculate, to not

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.580
make these little mistakes
that then cost you the points

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.690
even though you're actually
were on the right track,

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:45.970
you actually had all the numbers

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:47.730
maybe did all the calculations correct,

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:50.280
but just messed up by
just answering precisely,

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.120
what was being asked from you.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:54.430
So these are these
automated online assessments

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.370
which now get more and more popular

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:57.740
with these consulting firms,

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.850
but then it is all the firms that I heard

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:02.610
of still also conduct interviews person

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:06.010
by person and these take
place via video call

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:06.850
most of the time.

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:08.620
Now I heard of a couple of instances when

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:11.220
the first round also was
a telephone interview.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.020
And I also heard of instances
where the case interviews

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.630
is conducted on the telephone.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.630
So I personally believe
that this is quite crazy

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:19.740
because if you cannot even
look somebody in the eye

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:22.490
this is really difficult,
but this might happen to you.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.210
But then at least for the second round

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:27.090
for the more serious interviews,
there will be video calls.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:29.320
So most of them would
offer taking place on Zoom,

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.030
but I have also heard of these interviews

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:33.350
taking place on WebEx,
on Teams or whatever,

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.840
but here you can trust it
and the company will provide

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:38.420
the required infrastructure
for you to be able to join.

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:39.680
And then in these interviews,

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:41.703
all of these MBB consulting firms continue

00:06:41.703 --> 00:06:44.310
to use the two main interview types

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:45.760
which are also used in the part.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.420
And this is of course
first the case interview.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.100
So I will try to solve the case

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:51.590
that the interview is presenting for you.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.710
And then second, the behavioral part

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:56.830
or personal impact part or
personal experience part

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:58.290
or whatever the different names are

00:06:58.290 --> 00:06:59.557
that these companies come up for that.

00:06:59.557 --> 00:07:01.340
And this is the interview
we are confronted

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:03.311
with specific situations
that might've happened

00:07:03.311 --> 00:07:04.260
in your life.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.990
We are supposed to tell some stories how

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:07.880
you handle these situations in the past

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:09.860
and then they will evolve
for conversation around that.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:10.693
So here the bottom line is

00:07:10.693 --> 00:07:13.610
that this interview part
still is very similar

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:16.760
to how things were before the
current situation evolved.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:17.860
So if you want to prepare for that

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:20.185
look up all the information
that you find readily available

00:07:20.185 --> 00:07:23.080
on the internet, on how
to win in case interviews,

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.650
how to win in behavioral interviews.

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:26.820
This will still be very
much applicable, but still

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:29.200
I want to share two considerations
that are really special

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.990
about this online interview
video conference format.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:33.380
And the first is that of course,

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:35.280
because you're not sitting face to face

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:37.810
in a room, it would be much more difficult

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.823
to show the interviewer your notes

00:07:39.823 --> 00:07:42.310
because this is a common
tactic, especially

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:45.250
in case interviews to
make a very visual drawing

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.190
off your structure of the case

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.820
and then show it to the interviewer

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:51.170
and then have a discussion
based on your notes.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.010
This of course will be very difficult.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:55.280
So you might try whether
you can maybe hold it

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.210
in your webcam or based on the quality

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.600
of your webcam and also
how well the order focuses.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:02.150
It is very likely that this
will not really work away

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:03.950
that you will not be
really be able to show

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.230
your notes to the interviewer.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.870
So what this means is
that you need to be even

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:10.130
more deliberate, even more
salient, even more clear

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.800
and transparent about what
your thought processes.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.970
So guide the interviewer
through your thoughts,

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.210
really explain him the structure,

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:19.460
you need to put even
more emphasis on this.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:22.000
Then you might need to put
in a face-to-face interview

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.240
because you do not have the chance to show

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:25.740
the interviewer the notes anymore.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.720
And then the next advice
that I have, and here

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:29.600
especially if you know
you have a whole set

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:32.440
of interviews lined up for
the next weeks a month.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:36.870
Really try to invest into your
video conferencing equipment.

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:38.740
You would be surprised how many candidates

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:40.740
will sit there just with an old laptop

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:45.047
an old built-in webcam in the
laptop of not even full HD.

00:08:45.047 --> 00:08:47.610
And then also not really
using a proper microphone

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:49.890
but just the built-in mic
that comes with your laptop.

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:51.730
So while this might work and I trust

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.730
many people will also
be able to get offers

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:54.960
with such an equipment.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.280
One way to show your
professionalism, at least

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:59.930
on a subconscious level for the
interviewer, is to make sure

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.990
that you really have a good picture,

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:05.500
that you really have professional
audio, professional sound.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:08.060
So here, if you are
willing to invest a couple

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:10.650
of hundred bucks, this might be worthwhile

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.970
if you have a whole set of
interviews now lined up.

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:15.700
I would encourage you to
first upgrade your audio.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.450
I believe the audio will be
the most important factor

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:19.870
driving your impression,

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.530
and you can get some very decent USB mics

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:25.430
which are pretty much plug
and play 400 bucks or below.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:27.179
And then second if you
are willing to invest

00:09:27.179 --> 00:09:31.120
a little bit more, try to get
at least the full HD webcam.

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:33.793
And if you have a good incurrent DSLR,

00:09:33.793 --> 00:09:36.980
there are different options
to also use your DSLR

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:39.260
also mirror less camera as a webcam.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.760
And this of course would significantly

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.130
increase your picture quality.

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:44.200
And the third tip to
really improve your picture

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.900
with simple means is lighting.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:48.940
Even bad cameras will
always look much better,

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:50.790
if you have good lighting.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:53.160
Here again for 50 bucks or
so you could get yourself

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:55.060
a nice ring light one that I also

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:56.400
have here in front of me.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:57.730
This will put great light on you

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.287
and this will significantly improve

00:09:59.287 --> 00:10:01.620
the picture output that you have.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.040
And again, if you do all this

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:04.850
the interviewer will notice it.

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:06.910
Here's one candidate after each other,

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:09.590
all of them with crappy
audio, crappy video,

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:12.410
you know you suddenly
sitting there like a pro,

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:14.600
this will make some kind of impression.

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:15.830
This will show that you're serious

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:17.550
and that you have a professional mindset

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:19.460
when approaching these
types of situations.

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:22.490
So hope that this was helpful
